#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:42
#: d3bb1f45bd0d42c7886c60e442ad2764
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:43
#: 177ba66509804bf79414d33b7dca47d7
msgid "The RCIN pin, which by default is mapped to a timer input, can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, will only provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:45
#: d269e574757f4c0fa19518119cc19f3f
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, a full UART, such as SERIAL5 (UART3) would need to be used for receiver connections. Below are setups using Serial6. For the 6C Mini, SERIAL1 - SERIAL4 would need to be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:47
#: d08f9e0915934966a00a7e9331949d1d
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL5_PROTOCOL<SERIAL5_PROTOCOL>` should be set to \"23\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:49
#: f8c794e08c8e41c7bb1ebea3d8d7fa22
msgid "FPort would require :ref:`SERIAL5_OPTIONS<SERIAL5_OPTIONS>` be set to \"15\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:51
#: fcd9cc1882bc422daa7315ca2d0f0263
msgid "CRSF would require :ref:`SERIAL5_OPTIONS<SERIAL5_OPTIONS>` be set to \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:53
#: 79ee83e007214610b6634d50d37739aa
msgid "SRXL2 would require :ref:`SERIAL5_OPTIONS<SERIAL5_OPTIONS>` be set to \"4\" and connects only the TX pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:55
#: dd0faf5ac9994d28b312fde8e85fd6ef
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM. See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:58
#: b43714f42c2e49c8b902ce6dc65da8c3
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:60
#: 53934dd198274b01836b737c8815b0c5
msgid "The Pixhawk6C supports up to 16 PWM outputs. All 16 outputs support all normal PWM output formats. All FMU outputs (marked \"FMU PWM Output\") also support DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:63
#: 8063eedc44a244b38879ad63579a2018
msgid "The 8 FMU PWM outputs are in 4 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:65
#: 45c7fdc0a0d944c29ca5b54c589cfc32
msgid "PWM 1, 2, 3 and 4 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:66
#: 33a3ca5c48444f078e9041ab75c0d574
msgid "PWM 5 and 6 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:67
#: 1ed9a0b5b3774c4b969db735ade47ebc
msgid "PWM 7 and 8 in group3 (not 6C Mini)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:69
#: e2693570e2e54edb86c3ee2bb60c7101
msgid "FMU outputs within the same group need to use the same output rate and protocol. If any output in a group uses DShot then all channels in that group need to use DShot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-holybro-pixhawk6C.rst:73
#: 15908a52c1e144e4b258811963bd7f36
msgid "to use BDShot capability on outputs 1-8, use the firmware in the \"Pixhawk6C-bdshot\" folder on the `Firmware Server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__"
msgstr ""

